# File: /.gitattributes
# Purpose: Ensure binary assets are treated correctly by git
# Version: 1.0

*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# The AI assistants' notes are compared byte for byte by
# scripts/sync-ai-context.sh --check (the Codex copy in .OpenAI/ must match the
# Claude notes exactly). Git for Windows would otherwise check these out with
# Windows line endings, and the comparison would then report "out of step"
# even when nothing is. Always use plain Unix line endings for them. (2026-09-21, #202)
# Only .md files are named, never whole folders: a folder-wide rule would also
# apply to any image saved there and would silently alter it (a review proved
# this with a test image). Shell scripts need the same rule, or a Windows
# checkout breaks them outright ("set: -: invalid option").
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
.claude/**/*.md text eol=lf
.OpenAI/**/*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
